  "body": "**Blocked by:** #106\n\n## Context\n\nCore needs one typed contract for modules without module-id branches or runtime discovery.\n\n## Task\n\nDefine `ModuleManifest` with `id`, `version`, `name`, `removable`, `systemProject`, `databases`, `capabilities`, `agentTools`, optional `viewTypes`, `heartbeatActions`, `heartbeatRuleKinds`, `taskNames`, `workers`, and `migrations`. A task descriptor includes exactly `name`, `payloadSchemaExport`, and `handlerExport`; affinity-safe runtime ownership is deliberately added later by #91. Implement `ModuleRegistry.loadModule(path)` using an explicit known-path dynamic import. Validate duplicate identifiers and every named handler/schema export at load, failing startup loudly. Read `modules.active` at runtime. Expose only narrow typed projections for each aspect. Filter agent tools out entirely when their capability is absent.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Types, loading, activation, structural validation, projections, and capability filtering.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Directory scanning, hot installation, task registration, and runtime worker hosting.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Invalid exports and duplicate ids or names prevent startup; affinity validation is deferred to #91.\n- Inactive modules disappear from every projection.\n- No consumer API exposes the raw manifest.\n- Ungranted tools are absent rather than present-but-denied.\n",
